### What version of Codex CLI is running?

[Codex 0.155.1](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.155.1), the same issue remains in [Codex CLI prerelease 0.157.0-alpha.9](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.157.0-alpha.9).

### What subscription do you have?

Not applicable, no account was used.

### Which model were you using?

Not applicable, no model was used.

### What platform is your computer?

NixOS 26.05.

### What terminal emulator and version are you using (if applicable)?

Not applicable, native library tests.

### Codex doctor report

Not applicable, the reproduction uses library tests.

### What issue are you seeing?

Codex can use the second message as a conversation's preview after recovering from an error while saving the first. Both messages remain in the conversation history, but Codex incorrectly records the second as the first and uses it for the stored preview.

A conversation list using this preview could show a follow-up (such as "yes, continue") instead of the original request, making the conversation harder to identify.

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

Use the [0.155.1](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.155.1) source checkout, save the patch below as `append-recovery.patch`, then run from the checkout root:

```bash
git apply /absolute/path/to/append-recovery.patch
cd codex-rs
just test -p codex-thread-store append_recovery_ --no-capture
```

The patch adds tests using the real storage layer, recorder and SQLite, without changing production behaviour. Each test uses a fresh temporary home. The tests temporarily block creation of the history directory, attempt to save the first message, then remove the obstruction and flush the buffered message. They append a second message and compare the saved history with the conversation metadata.

<details>
<summary>Reproduction test patch</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/mod.rs b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/mod.rs
--- a/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/mod.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/mod.rs
@@ -734,6 +734,8 @@
 #[cfg(test)]
 mod tests {
+    #[path = "append_recovery_tests.rs"]
+    mod append_recovery_tests;
     use std::sync::Arc;

     use codex_protocol::ThreadId;
     use codex_protocol::config_types::ReasoningSummary;
diff --git a/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/tests/append_recovery_tests.rs b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/tests/append_recovery_tests.rs
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/tests/append_recovery_tests.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,178 @@
+//! Fixture-owned persistence recovery: real recorder, LiveThread and SQLite.
+//! No production behavior is modified; all paths belong to one fresh TempDir.
+use super::*;
+use codex_protocol::user_input::UserInput;
+use pretty_assertions::assert_eq;
+use serde_json::json;
+
+async fn scenario(history_mode: ThreadHistoryMode, recover_first_append: bool) {
+    let home = TempDir::new().expect("owned temporary Codex home");
+    let config = test_config(home.path());
+    let runtime = codex_state::StateRuntime::init(
+        config.sqlite.clone(),
+        config.default_model_provider_id.clone(),
+    )
+    .await
+    .expect("initialize fixture SQLite");
+    let store = Arc::new(LocalThreadStore::new(config, Some(runtime.clone())));
+    let thread_id = ThreadId::new();
+    let mut params = create_thread_params(thread_id);
+    params.history_mode = history_mode;
+    params.metadata.cwd = Some(home.path().to_path_buf());
+    let live = LiveThread::create(store.clone(), params)
+        .await
+        .expect("create managed deferred thread");
+    let rollout_path = store
+        .live_rollout_path(thread_id)
+        .await
+        .expect("rollout path");
+    assert!(
+        !rollout_path.exists(),
+        "fixture starts before materialization"
+    );
+    let input = |text: &str, turn: &str| match history_mode {
+        ThreadHistoryMode::Legacy => user_message_item(text),
+        ThreadHistoryMode::Paginated => {
+            RolloutItem::EventMsg(EventMsg::ItemCompleted(ItemCompletedEvent {
+                thread_id,
+                turn_id: turn.to_string(),
+                item: TurnItem::UserMessage(UserMessageItem::new(&[UserInput::Text {
+                    text: text.to_string(),
+                    text_elements: Vec::new(),
+                }])),
+                started_at_ms: Some(0),
+                completed_at_ms: 1,
+            }))
+        }
+    };
+    let sessions = home.path().join("sessions");
+    if recover_first_append {
+        // Same filesystem-error condition as existing recorder retry coverage.
+        std::fs::write(&sessions, b"fixture temporary directory obstruction")
+            .expect("create owned temporary obstruction");
+    }
+    let first_result = live
+        .append_items(&[input("first fixture message", "turn-1")])
+        .await;
+    let first_error = first_result.as_ref().err().map(ToString::to_string);
+    if recover_first_append {
+        assert!(
+            first_result.is_err(),
+            "first append must report filesystem error"
+        );
+        assert!(
+            !rollout_path.exists(),
+            "failed append did not materialize history"
+        );
+        std::fs::remove_file(&sessions).expect("restore owned fixture path");
+    } else {
+        first_result.expect("healthy append");
+    }
+    live.flush().await.expect("recover buffered append");
+    live.flush().await.expect("repeat recovery barrier");
+    let (recovered, _, _) = RolloutRecorder::load_rollout_items(&rollout_path)
+        .await
+        .expect("read recovered canonical history");
+    let messages = |items: Vec<RolloutItem>| {
+        items
+            .into_iter()
+            .filter_map(|item| match item {
+                RolloutItem::EventMsg(EventMsg::UserMessage(user)) => Some(user.message),
+                RolloutItem::EventMsg(EventMsg::ItemCompleted(event)) => match event.item {
+                    TurnItem::UserMessage(user) => Some(user.message()),
+                    _ => None,
+                },
+                _ => None,
+            })
+            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
+    };
+    let recovered_messages = messages(recovered);
+    let metadata_after_recovery = runtime.get_thread(thread_id).await.expect("metadata read");
+    live.append_items(&[input("second fixture message", "turn-2")])
+        .await
+        .expect("second append succeeds");
+    live.flush().await.expect("flush second append");
+    let metadata_after_second = runtime
+        .get_thread(thread_id)
+        .await
+        .expect("metadata read after second input")
+        .expect("thread metadata exists");
+    let public_thread = store
+        .read_thread(ReadThreadParams {
+            thread_id,
+            include_archived: false,
+            include_history: false,
+        })
+        .await
+        .expect("read public thread metadata");
+    live.shutdown()
+        .await
+        .expect("close fixture writer normally");
+    let (final_history, _, _) = RolloutRecorder::load_rollout_items(&rollout_path)
+        .await
+        .expect("read final history");
+    let final_messages = messages(final_history);
+    eprintln!(
+        "APPEND_RECOVERY_OBSERVATION {}",
+        json!({
+            "history_mode": history_mode,
+            "recover_first_append": recover_first_append,
+            "first_append_error": first_error,
+            "recovered_messages": recovered_messages,
+            "metadata_after_recovery": metadata_after_recovery.as_ref().map(|m| json!({
+                "first_user_message": m.first_user_message, "preview": m.preview, "title": m.title,
+            })),
+            "metadata_after_second": {
+                "first_user_message": metadata_after_second.first_user_message,
+                "preview": metadata_after_second.preview, "title": metadata_after_second.title,
+            },
+            "public_after_second": {
+                "first_user_message": public_thread.first_user_message,
+                "preview": public_thread.preview, "name": public_thread.name,
+            },
+            "final_messages": final_messages,
+        })
+    );
+    assert_eq!(recovered_messages, vec!["first fixture message"]);
+    assert_eq!(
+        final_messages,
+        vec!["first fixture message", "second fixture message"]
+    );
+    if history_mode == ThreadHistoryMode::Legacy {
+        assert_eq!(
+            public_thread.first_user_message.as_deref(),
+            Some("first fixture message")
+        );
+        assert_eq!(public_thread.preview, "first fixture message");
+    }
+    // Desired managed-metadata invariant, after recording all observations and cleanup.
+    assert_eq!(
+        metadata_after_second.first_user_message.as_deref(),
+        Some("first fixture message"),
+        "successful recovery must not let the second message replace the first in SQLite metadata"
+    );
+    assert_eq!(
+        public_thread.first_user_message.as_deref(),
+        Some("first fixture message")
+    );
+}
+
+#[tokio::test]
+async fn append_recovery_legacy_healthy_control() {
+    scenario(ThreadHistoryMode::Legacy, false).await;
+}
+
+#[tokio::test]
+async fn append_recovery_legacy_recovered_append_keeps_first_metadata() {
+    scenario(ThreadHistoryMode::Legacy, true).await;
+}
+
+#[tokio::test]
+async fn append_recovery_paginated_healthy_control() {
+    scenario(ThreadHistoryMode::Paginated, false).await;
+}
+
+#[tokio::test]
+async fn append_recovery_paginated_recovered_append_keeps_first_metadata() {
+    scenario(ThreadHistoryMode::Paginated, true).await;
+}
```

</details>

With the bug present, both recovery tests fail at the first-message metadata assertion, while both healthy controls pass.

| After the second append | Actual value |
| --- | --- |
| Saved history | First message, then second message; neither duplicated |
| SQLite first message / preview / initial title | Second message |
| Paginated read first message / preview | Second message |
| Legacy read first message / preview | First message |

The legacy reader gets the correct preview from the history file, despite the incorrect SQLite metadata.

### What is the expected behavior?

When the first message is saved after recovery, its metadata should recover with it. A later message should not replace it as the conversation's first message or preview.

### Additional information

#### Root cause analysis

Recovery saves the buffered message, but does not update the state used to derive its metadata:

1. [`LiveThread::append_items()`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/thread-store/src/live_thread.rs#L203) awaits `persist_appended_items(...)?` before calling `observe_appended_items()`. If persistence returns an error, the method exits before the message is used to update metadata.
2. However, [`durable_write()`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/live_writer.rs#L362) queues the message before waiting for the recorder to flush it to storage. The error therefore doesn't necessarily mean the message was rejected.
3. The [recorder retains unwritten messages](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/rollout/src/recorder.rs#L1795-L1850), allowing a later `flush()` to save the first message successfully.
4. [`LiveThread::flush()`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/thread-store/src/live_thread.rs#L268) retries persistence and any already-pending metadata update. It doesn't repeat the observation skipped by the failed append, so there is no pending first-message update to apply.
5. When the second message arrives successfully, [`observe_user_message()`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/thread-store/src/thread_metadata_sync.rs#L321) still has no record of observing a first message. It therefore uses the second message to initialise the first-message metadata, preview and initial title.

The [legacy display fallback](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be2951ea34f0d295ed0becf97079f92fa5f6950e/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/read_thread.rs#L53-L65) hides the stored mismatch from that mode's reader. The paginated read exposes it.

#### Suggested fix

I'd suggest retaining the pending metadata observation for messages accepted by the recorder, so `LiveThread::flush()` can apply it when recovery saves them. Each message should be observed once, rejected messages should not create metadata.
